17 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows a Bland-Altman plot comparing the difference between predictions and observed values of ml per min per kg against their mean, with data points, mean line at approximately -0.08, and limits of agreement at plus 5.63 and minus 5.79. Panel b shows a similar Bland-Altman plot with a mean near 0.09, and limits of agreement at plus 5.67 and minus 5.49.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Two SHAP summary dot plots labeled \215a\216 and \215b\216 display the impact of various features on model outputs. Each horizontal axis shows SHAP value ranges from negative two to seven. The vertical axis lists features such as Age, FATP, Experience_in_years, Maturity, and others. Dots colored from blue to red represent feature value magnitudes, with blue indicating low and red indicating high, alongside a colorbar labeled \215Feature value.\216 Age, FATP, and Experience_in_years appear most influential in both plots, as their dots are most widely distributed along the SHAP value axis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
